<header>
    <h1>Personal Profile</h1>
</header>

<main>

    <section class="profile">

        <aside class="profile-picture">
            <img src="/static/Personal-Profile.jpg" alt="Student Profile">
        </aside>

        <!-- About Me -->
        <section class="about">
            <p>
                My name is Thomas Hunt, and I am a Year 11 student at Sacred Heart College.
                I enjoy rowing, gaming, drawing and coding. Computer Science is one of my
                favourite subjects because I want to become a software engineer in the future.
                In my free time, I also enjoy playing games like Minecraft, Fortnite, Roblox,
                and Plants vs. Zombies.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Catholic Perspective -->
        <section class="catholic">
            <p>
                From a Catholic Perspective, I believe every person has dignity because they
                are created in the image of God. In the digital age, we have a social duty to
                treat others with respect, kindness, and responsibility online. This means
                avoiding cyberbullying, protecting others' privacy and using technology to
                help others.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Hobbies -->
        <section class="hobbies">
            <h2>Hobbies / Interests</h2>

            <div class="hobby-content">
                <ul>
                    <li>Rowing</li>
                    <li>Gaming</li>
                    <li>Coding</li>
                    <li>Drawing</li>
                </ul>

                <ul>
                    <li>Basketball</li>
                    <li>Gaming (Sometimes)</li>
                    <li>Playing UNO</li>
                    <li>Playing Clarinet</li>
                </ul>

                <img src="/static/Rowing-Image.jpeg" alt="Rowing">
            </div>
        </section>

    </section>

    <!-- Social Media -->
    <section class="info-box">
        <h2>Social Media and My Generation</h2>

        <p>
            Social media is a big part of my generation’s everyday life, helping us communicate,
            share ideas, and stay connected. However, it can also cause problems such as
            cyberbullying, pressure, misinformation, and stress. Personally, I think social
            media can be useful and entertaining when it is used responsibly and in moderation.
            It is important to maintain a healthy balance between online and real life.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="info-box pope">
        <h2>Pope Francis and his teaching</h2>

        <p>
            Pope Francis teaches that social media can be a positive way to communicate and
            connect with others, but it can also cause problems such as addiction, isolation,
            cyberbullying, and misinformation. In Christus Vivit, he encourages young people
            to use technology responsibly and not allow online relationships to replace
            genuine human connections.
        </p>
    </section>

</main>

